---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import { company, site, power, network, compute, publicDeployment as deployment } from '../data/site';
---
<Content
  title={`B300 compute in Mead, Oklahoma | ${company.full}`}
  description={`SmartTec proposes ${deployment.gpus} B300 GPUs in ${deployment.systems} complete Supermicro systems at ${site.designation}. Explore the workload, liquid-cooling and commissioning plan.`}
  kicker="B300 compute / Proposed deployment"
  heading="Build around the workload."
  lede={`Our proposed initial fleet brings ${deployment.gpus} B300 GPUs together in ${deployment.systems} complete Supermicro systems, in one building at ${site.name}. Direct liquid cooling is required, and all cooling will be new. Customer commitments, complete costs and engineering acceptance determine procurement and service availability.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Proposed B300 GPUs', value: String(deployment.gpus), note: 'Planning count, not available inventory', count: true, tone: 'signal' },
    { label: 'Complete systems', value: String(deployment.systems), note: `${deployment.gpusPerSystem} B300 GPUs per Supermicro system`, count: true },
    { label: 'Location', value: 'One building', note: 'Final A or C allocation pending' },
    { label: 'Deployment status', value: 'Proposed', note: 'Procurement and commissioning ahead', tone: 'gold' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="fleet" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Initial fleet proposal</span></p>
    <h2 id="fleet">Eight systems. A complete deployment to validate.</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card__tag mono-label">{deployment.systems} complete Supermicro systems</p>
        <h3>NVIDIA B300 compute</h3>
        <p>Each proposed system contains {deployment.gpusPerSystem} B300 GPUs. {deployment.scope}</p>
        <p>External networking, storage, installation and ongoing service obligations must be reconciled with the full deployment requirements.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card__tag mono-label">Proposed allocation</p>
        <h3>{deployment.saleableGpus} saleable + {deployment.reserveGpus} reserve</h3>
        <p>{deployment.reserveNote}</p>
        <p>Scheduling, maintenance and node-failure recovery need validation before we offer a service level. These GPUs are not currently bookable inventory.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--s-6);">
      <p><strong>Commercial stage.</strong> {deployment.demand} Customer availability follows procurement, workload validation and facility and network acceptance.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="configuration" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Match the workload</span></p>
    <h2 id="configuration">Choose capacity around the job.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>Tell us the application, model size, memory needs, storage throughput and intended software stack. We assess the required GPU allocation, networking, security, support and service targets against a representative workload.</p>
        <p>Inference, rendering and suitable fine-tuning require different software and performance tests. A GPU count alone does not establish throughput, latency or a customer outcome.</p>
        <p>The model planner compares hardware reference configurations. Its memory and power estimates do not certify the proposed fleet or the facility design.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>Initial proposal</dt><dd>{deployment.systems} systems × {deployment.gpusPerSystem} B300 GPUs<span class="note">{deployment.gpus} GPUs in total; planning status.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Cooling requirement</dt><dd>Direct liquid cooling<span class="note">Confirmed by management for the selected server requirement; plant design and acceptance remain open.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Building allocation</dt><dd>One building<span class="note">The eight systems will be together. Which building and final rack layout remain to be established.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Power allocation</dt><dd>Engineering review pending<span class="note">No measured OEM load or exclusive continuous site capacity is established by this proposal.</span></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/model-planner">Explore model requirements</a></div>
    <p class="form-note">RTX remains an alternative requiring its own workload and commercial case. The homepage's RTX-only estimator retains the earlier {compute.servers}-node, {compute.gpus}-GPU example; it does not size the current B300 proposal.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="cooling" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Campus integration</span></p>
    <h2 id="cooling">Designed with power and cooling.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>{power.hvac} We are comparing new and warranted refurbished cooling plant, conventional room cooling and rear-door heat exchangers. Separate dry coolers are an optional later economizer investment, subject to design and operating economics.</p>
        <p>The two-duty cooling concept can use a shared plant with separately controlled circuits. Final equipment count, temperatures, residual-air capacity and redundancy require mechanical and OEM acceptance.</p>
        <p>The campus electrical commissioning milestone is an {power.commissioningTarget}. Planned {network.provider} fiber has an {network.deliveryTarget}. These management targets are distinct from completed customer service acceptance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Explore the infrastructure</h3>
        <p>Review the behind-the-meter supply strategy, shared electrical service and cooling options. Detailed funding and operating assumptions are in the investor room.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a href="/power#thermal">Power and cooling →</a><a href="/investors">Investor room →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="buying" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Start a conversation</span></p>
    <h2 id="buying">Bring us your workload.</h2>
    <p>We review platform fit, capacity, timing and support needs, then develop a proposal with the configuration and commercial terms. You can also discuss colocation for hardware you already own.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Discuss compute requirements</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/colocation">Explore colocation</a></div>
  </section>
</Content>
